(guard (e (#t #f))
  (jv$clojure.core/attach-core-doc-meta! "clojure.core" "halt-when" "Returns a transducer that ends transduction when pred returns true\n  for an input. When retf is supplied it must be a fn of 2 arguments -\n  it will be passed the (completed) result so far and the input that\n  triggered the predicate, and its return value (if it does not throw\n  an exception) will be the return value of the transducer. If retf\n  is not supplied, the input that triggered the predicate will be\n  returned. If the predicate never returns true the transduction is\n  unaffected." (jolt-list (jolt-vector (jolt-symbol #f "pred")) (jolt-vector (jolt-symbol #f "pred") (jolt-symbol #f "retf"))) jolt-nil))
